  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Aeschylus was one of the rock stars of ancient Athens, a founding father of Greek tragedy.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "greek",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "aeschylus",
      "x": 0.5,
      "pose": "present",
      "hold": "scroll"
     }
    ],
    "tag": {
     "id": "aeschylus",
     "text": "Aeschylus"
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "He wrote dozens of plays, seven of which still survive, and he fought the Persians at the Battle of Marathon."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "According to Aristotle, he was also the guy who first put a second actor on stage, which means before Aeschylus, Greek drama was basically one actor and a chorus."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Around 456 BC, he died in the town of Gela, on the island of Sicily."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "And according to a story told by later Roman writers, here's how."
  },
  {
   "who": "greekfriend",
   "say": "Aeschylus, why are you sitting outside again?",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "field",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "greekfriend",
      "x": 0.3,
      "pose": "shrug"
     },
     {
      "id": "aeschylus",
      "x": 0.7,
      "pose": "sit"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "aeschylus",
   "say": "A prophecy says something will fall on me and kill me. So, no roofs. I'm very safe out here."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Pliny the Elder writes that Aeschylus was staying outdoors to dodge a prophecy like that."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Meanwhile, high above, an eagle had caught a tortoise, and it was looking for a nice hard rock to crack it open on.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "field",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "aeschylus",
      "x": 0.5,
      "pose": "sit",
      "mood": "happy"
     }
    ],
    "cam": "pan",
    "stickers": [
     {
      "text": "EAGLE",
      "at": 0.8,
      "color": "#6A4A2A"
     },
     {
      "text": "+ TORTOISE",
      "at": 1.8,
      "color": "#1F8A4A"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "From way up there, it spotted something smooth, shiny and round."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Of all the places in the Mediterranean to drop a tortoise. I mean, what are the odds?"
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Aeschylus's bald head.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "field",
    "cast": [
     {
