  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "The next morning, Attila didn't come out, so his guards finally broke down the door.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "night",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "hunguard",
      "x": 0.5,
      "pose": "scared",
      "mood": "shock"
     }
    ],
    "cam": "shake"
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "According to the historian Priscus, whose account was preserved by Jordanes, Attila had a heavy nosebleed while lying on his back, full of wine, and it choked him."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "He terrorized half of Europe, and he was taken out by his own nose."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Imagine being the guard who had to walk outside and explain that one."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Some historians have wondered if it was secretly an assassination, but there's no solid evidence either way."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Jordanes adds that Attila was buried in three coffins, one of gold, one of silver and one of iron, and nobody has ever found them.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "steppe",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "hunguard",
      "x": 0.5,
      "pose": "shrug"
