  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Then, in 1555, he finally won Delhi back.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "palace",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "humayun",
      "x": 0.5,
      "pose": "cheer",
      "mood": "happy"
     }
    ],
    "fx": [
     "confetti"
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "And what did he love more than almost anything? Books."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Seriously, he was a huge reader, and he was obsessed with astronomy too."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "His library was a two-story building called the Sher Mandal, and it had some seriously steep stairs.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "library",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "humayun",
      "x": 0.5,
      "pose": "hold",
      "mood": "happy"
     }
    ],
    "cam": "pan",
    "stickers": [
     {
      "text": "STEEP STAIRS",
      "at": 1.5,
      "color": "#3A4A8A"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "One evening in January 1556, he was heading down those stairs when he heard the call to prayer."
  },
  {
   "who": "humayun",
   "say": "Ah, the call to prayer. I'll just kneel right here on the step.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "library",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "humayun",
      "pose": "sit"
     }
    ],
    "cam": "close",
    "focus": "humayun"
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "When he got back up, his foot caught in his robe, and down he went.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "library",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "humayun",
      "x": 0.5,
      "pose": "scared",
      "mood": "shock"
     }
    ],
    "cam": "shake",
    "stickers": [
     {
      "text": "TUMBLE",
      "at": 0.8,
      "color": "#A8322A"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "He hit his head and died a few days later, only about six months after getting his empire back."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "The historian Stanley Lane-Poole summed it up: Humayun tumbled through life, and he tumbled out of it."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "And the Sher Mandal is still standing in Delhi's Old Fort today, stairs and all. Watch your step."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "His thirteen-year-old son Akbar took over, and went on to become one of the greatest emperors in Indian history.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "throne",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "akbar",
      "x": 0.5,
      "pose": "hips",
      "mood": "smug"
     }
    ],
    "tag": {
     "id": "akbar",
     "text": "Akbar"
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "hold": 2.5,
   "show": {
    "k": "list",
    "n": "5",
    "title": "Death by Conducting"
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Number five: Jean-Baptiste Lully, the superstar composer at the court of King Louis the Fourteenth.",
   "show": {
    "k": "map",
    "lon": 2.35,
    "lat": 48.85,
    "z0": 2.5,
    "z1": 3.5,
    "date": "1687",
    "labels": [
     [
      "Paris",
      2.35,
      48.85,
      0
     ],
     [
      "Versailles",
      2.12,
      48.8,
      -40
     ]
    ],
    "areas": [
     [
      2.35,
      48.85,
      0.3,
      "rgba(200,60,40,0.35)"
     ]
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Lully was in charge of the king's music, which basically made him the boss of French music, and he knew it.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "palace",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "lully",
      "x": 0.35,
      "pose": "present",
      "mood": "smug"
     },
     {
      "id": "louis",
      "x": 0.7,
      "pose": "hips"
     }
    ],
    "tag": {
     "id": "lully",
     "text": "Jean-Baptiste Lully"
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "With the king's backing, he even held a monopoly on opera in France, so if you wanted to stage one, you basically had to go through Lully."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Back then, conductors didn't wave a little baton; they kept time by banging a long, heavy staff on the floor."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "In January 1687, Lully conducted his Te Deum to celebrate the king recovering from surgery.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "church",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "lully",
      "x": 0.5,
      "pose": "fist",
      "mood": "happy"
     }
    ],
    "stickers": [
     {
      "text": "BANG",
      "at": 0.8,
      "color": "#3A4A8A"
     },
     {
      "text": "BANG",
      "at": 1.6,
      "color": "#3A4A8A"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "lully",
   "say": "And one, and two, and one, and..."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Then he brought the staff down right on his own foot.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "church",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "lully",
      "x": 0.5,
      "pose": "scared",
      "mood": "shock"
     }
    ],
    "cam": "shake",
    "stickers": [
     {
      "text": "OW!",
      "at": 0.4,
      "color": "#A8322A"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "The wound got infected, and it turned into gangrene."
  },
  {
   "who": "physician",
   "say": "Monsieur, we must remove the toe. Perhaps more.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "office",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "physician",
      "x": 0.3,
      "pose": "point"
     },
     {
      "id": "lully",
      "x": 0.7,
      "pose": "cross",
      "mood": "angry"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "lully",
   "say": "Absolutely not. I am a dancer!"
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "The story goes that Lully refused an amputation, partly because he wanted to keep dancing."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "He died on the twenty-second of March, 1687, killed, more or less, by his own music."
  },
  {
   "hold": 2.5,
   "show": {
    "k": "list",
    "n": "4",
    "title": "The King Who Ate Himself to Death"
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Number four: King Adolf Frederick of Sweden.",
   "show": {
    "k": "map",
    "lon": 18.07,
    "lat": 59.33,
    "z0": 2.0,
    "z1": 3.2,
    "date": "1771",
    "labels": [
     [
      "Stockholm",
      18.07,
      59.33,
      0
     ],
     [
      "Sweden",
      15.0,
      62.0,
      0
     ]
    ],
    "areas": [
     [
      18.07,
      59.33,
      0.4,
      "rgba(200,60,40,0.35)"
     ]
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Sweden's parliament held most of the real power in his day, so the king had plenty of free time, and a famous hobby: making snuffboxes.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "throne",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "adolf",
      "x": 0.5,
      "pose": "sit",
      "mood": "happy"
     }
    ],
    "tag": {
     "id": "adolf",
     "text": "King Adolf Frederick"
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "On the twelfth of February, 1771, it was Fat Tuesday, the last big feast before Lent."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "And the king went all in. Honestly, respect."
  },
  {
   "who": "chef",
   "say": "First course, Your Majesty: lobster, caviar and sauerkraut.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "palace",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "chef",
      "x": 0.3,
      "pose": "present"
     },
     {
      "id": "adolf",
      "x": 0.7,
      "pose": "cheer",
      "mood": "happy"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "adolf",
   "say": "Excellent. Keep it coming!"
  },
  {
   "who": "chef",
   "say": "Then smoked herring, and champagne."
  },
  {
   "who": "adolf",
   "say": "And now, dessert!"
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Dessert was semla, a sweet cream bun that Swedes still eat on Fat Tuesday, and back then it was served in a bowl of hot milk.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "palace",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "adolf",
      "x": 0.5,
      "pose": "hold",
      "mood": "happy"
     }
    ],
    "cam": "close",
    "focus": "adolf",
    "stickers": [
     {
      "text": "SEMLA",
      "at": 1.0,
      "color": "#C9A04A"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "hold": 3,
   "show": {
    "k": "card",
    "label": "Semla buns for dessert, reportedly",
    "big": "14",
    "sub": "The palace records are missing, so call it legend",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "adolf",
      "x": 0.82,
      "mood": "happy"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Legend says he ate fourteen of them."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "A few hours later, the king was dead.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "palace",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "adolf",
      "x": 0.5,
      "pose": "sit",
      "mood": "sad"
     }
    ],
    "cam": "still"
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "A month later, a young count who wasn't even at the dinner wrote in his diary that the king died of indigestion from hot semla, sauerkraut, lobster, caviar, duckling and champagne."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "The fourteen buns part only shows up much later, and he was sixty and in poor health, and his doctors blamed a stroke, but in Sweden he's still the king who ate himself to death."
  },
  {
   "hold": 2.5,
   "show": {
    "k": "list",
    "n": "3",
    "title": "Too Polite to Pee"
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Number three: Tycho Brahe, the Danish astronomer who mapped the stars better than anyone before the telescope.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "night",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "tycho",
      "x": 0.5,
      "pose": "point",
      "mood": "happy"
     }
    ],
    "fx": [
     "sparkle"
    ],
    "tag": {
     "id": "tycho",
     "text": "Tycho Brahe"
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Tycho was already a legend: he lost part of his nose in a sword duel as a student, and wore a metal replacement for the rest of his life.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "night",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "tycho",
      "mood": "smug"
     }
    ],
    "cam": "close",
    "focus": "tycho",
    "stickers": [
     {
      "text": "METAL NOSE",
      "at": 1.0,
      "color": "#C9A04A"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "He also reportedly had a pet elk that drank too much beer and died falling down a flight of stairs. Humayun would understand."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "In 1601, Tycho was working in Prague for the emperor, with a young assistant named Johannes Kepler.",
   "show": {
    "k": "map",
    "lon": 14.42,
    "lat": 50.08,
    "z0": 2.2,
    "z1": 3.2,
    "date": "1601",
    "labels": [
     [
      "Prague",
      14.42,
      50.08,
      0
     ],
     [
      "Denmark",
      10.0,
      56.0,
      0
     ]
    ],
    "areas": [
     [
      14.42,
      50.08,
      0.35,
      "rgba(200,60,40,0.35)"
     ]
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "That October, Tycho went to a fancy banquet hosted by a nobleman named Rosenberg.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "castle",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "tycho",
      "x": 0.35,
      "pose": "sit",
      "mood": "happy"
     },
     {
      "id": "rosenberg",
      "x": 0.7,
      "pose": "present"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "rosenberg",
   "say": "More wine, Tycho?"
  },
  {
   "who": "tycho",
   "say": "Oh, yes, thank you!"
  },
  {
   "who": "tycho",
   "say": "I really need to go. But leaving the table now would be so rude.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "castle",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "tycho",
      "pose": "sit",
      "mood": "scared"
     }
    ],
    "cam": "close",
    "focus": "tycho"
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "According to Kepler, Tycho held it in rather than break etiquette.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "office",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "kepler",
      "x": 0.5,
      "pose": "hold",
      "hold": "pen"
     }
    ],
    "tag": {
     "id": "kepler",
     "text": "Johannes Kepler"
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "By the time he got home, he couldn't go at all."
  },
  {
   "hold": 3,
   "show": {
    "k": "card",
    "label": "Prague, October 1601",
    "big": "11 DAYS",
    "sub": "from the banquet to Tycho's death",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "tycho",
      "x": 0.82,
      "mood": "sad"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Eleven days later, Tycho Brahe was dead."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Now, historians argue about this one: modern studies point to a bladder, kidney or prostate problem, and the banquet may have just been the last straw."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "And no, it wasn't poison: when scientists dug him up in 2010, they found nowhere near enough mercury to kill him."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "The good news: Kepler got his hands on Tycho's decades of star data, and used it to work out that planets orbit the sun in ellipses."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "So the lesson is clear. If you need to go, go."
  },
  {
   "hold": 2.5,
   "show": {
    "k": "list",
    "n": "2",
    "title": "The Lawyer Who Proved His Point"
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Number two: remember our lawyer from the start? His name was Clement Vallandigham, and he was one of the most famous politicians in Ohio.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "courtroom",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "vall",
      "x": 0.5,
      "pose": "point",
      "mood": "angry"
     }
    ],
    "tag": {
     "id": "vall",
     "text": "Clement Vallandigham"
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "During the Civil War, he attacked the Union war effort so loudly that he was arrested and literally shipped off to the Confederacy.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "town",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "vall",
      "x": 0.5,
      "pose": "walk",
      "walk": [
       0.3,
       0.8
      ],
      "mood": "angry"
     }
    ],
    "stickers": [
     {
      "text": "BANISHED",
      "at": 1.2,
      "color": "#A8322A"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "He even ran for governor of Ohio in 1863 while living in exile in Canada. He lost. Badly."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "After the war, he went back to being a lawyer, and a very good one."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "In June 1871, he was defending a man named Thomas McGehan, accused of shooting another man during a bar fight.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "courtroom",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "mcgehan",
      "x": 0.3,
      "pose": "shrug",
      "mood": "scared"
     },
     {
      "id": "judge",
      "x": 0.72,
      "pose": "cross"
     }
    ],
    "tag": {
     "id": "mcgehan",
     "text": "Thomas McGehan"
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "His defense: the victim had accidentally shot himself while pulling his own pistol out of his pocket as he stood up."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "At his hotel in Lebanon, Ohio, he decided to show his fellow lawyers exactly how it could have happened.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "tavern",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "vall",
      "x": 0.35,
      "pose": "present"
     },
     {
      "id": "lawyer",
      "x": 0.72,
      "pose": "think"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "lawyer",
   "say": "Clem, is that thing loaded?"
  },
  {
   "who": "vall",
   "say": "No, no. This is the empty one.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "tavern",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "vall",
      "pose": "hips",
      "mood": "smug"
     }
    ],
    "cam": "close",
    "focus": "vall"
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "It was not the empty one.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "tavern",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "vall",
      "x": 0.4,
      "pose": "scared",
      "mood": "shock"
     },
     {
      "id": "lawyer",
      "x": 0.72,
      "mood": "shock"
     }
    ],
    "cam": "shake",
    "fx": [
     "smoke"
    ],
    "stickers": [
     {
      "text": "BANG!",
      "at": 0.3,
      "color": "#A8322A"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "The pistol snagged on his clothes and went off, and he died the next day, at fifty."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "But here's the twist: the demonstration kind of worked."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "McGehan was eventually acquitted.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "courtroom",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "mcgehan",
      "x": 0.5,
      "pose": "cheer",
      "mood": "happy"
     }
    ],
    "fx": [
     "confetti"
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "His client walked free. Vallandigham just wasn't there to see it."
  },
  {
   "hold": 2.5,
   "show": {
    "k": "list",
    "n": "1",
    "title": "The Monkey Bite That Changed History"
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "And number one: King Alexander of Greece.",
   "show": {
    "k": "map",
    "lon": 23.75,
    "lat": 38.1,
    "z0": 2.5,
    "z1": 3.6,
    "date": "1920",
